Subject: [PATCH] docs(bot-mode): correct Bot Chat delivery argv, DM stamp and
 room store name
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three Bot Mode / Bot Chat statements no longer match the code on main:

- cron-internals.md gave the unowned cron delivery lane as
  `hermes [-p <profile>] chat ...`. _deliver_to_bot_chat
  (cron/scheduler_delivery.py) never passes the target profile with -p: it
  pins HERMES_HOME to the resolved target via served_profile_child_env and
  adds `-p default` only when the target is the root home.
- The zh-Hans bot-mode page showed the message_agent attribution as
  `Message from 🤖 <sender> (@<sender>):`. tools/bot_mode_dm.py stamps the
  sender's display name and handle, which the English page already shows
  as `<friendly name> (@<handle>)`.
- bot-mode.md (EN and zh-Hans) named the diverging per-gateway room stores
  `state.db`. Hosted-room coordination lives in the root shared-state.db
  (gateway/hosted_rooms.py default_db_path), deliberately separate from
  the master state.db.

Docs only; no behaviour change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
